  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "Because poker rewards are terminal and the inherited critic can bias short-horizon bootstrapped advantages, setting GAE lambda to 1.0 will give the actor exact discounted full-hand Monte-Carlo credit and improve robust learned-policy strength over the untouched lambda-0.95 all-heads control.",
  "material_change": "Change only --gae-lambda from the default 0.95 to 1.0. Retain Standard10 initialization, global advantage normalization, frozen representation, both policy heads, optimizer, fixed three-anchor adaptive league, training seeds/deals, actual-hand budget, and frozen evaluation schedule from adaptive-league-all-heads-pilot-20260830.",
  "baseline": "adaptive-league-all-heads-pilot-20260830 untouched lambda-0.95 all-policy-heads control",
  "source": "Terminal-only reward structure and repeated failure of variance, replay, league-selection, and representation-capacity treatments motivate isolating critic-bootstrap bias in actor credit.",
  "parent_id": "mirrored-selfplay-deals-pilot-20260830",
